liblockdc_postgres is licensed under the project MIT license.
It uses the public cpktdb PostgreSQL C89 facade and official dependency targets.

Consumed SDK releases: cpkt @LOCKDC_CPKT_VERSION@, cpktdb @LOCKDC_CPKTDB_VERSION@.
Original SDK manifests in sdk-provenance/ record their build and payload identity.
Their complete inventories describe those SDK bundles, including components this
provider does not link. They are provenance, not this provider's runtime inventory.

The PostgreSQL closure includes the cpktdb facade, PostgreSQL/libpq and its OAuth
support, plus cpkt OpenLDAP, SASL/Kerberos, curl, OpenSSL and zlib dependencies.
Curl also uses cpkt nghttp2 and libssh2. Native and system closures are supplied
by their official imported targets for the selected platform. This installation
does not copy third-party library payloads; supply the independent cpkt/cpktdb
SDKs and preserve their licenses when redistributing a linked application.

Complete upstream license texts are provided in licenses/. Core liblockdc and
its additional dependencies retain their separate existing notices/provenance.
